# Line endings that are part of the BUILD OUTPUT, not just a diff nuisance.
#
# Razor MARKUP WHITESPACE is embedded in the assembly as string content -- the
# generated App/Index BuildRenderTree hand their literal markup (including
# Index.razor's multi-line style="..." attribute) to AddMarkupContent, newlines
# and all. So a .razor file's ON-DISK EOL changes EvilAliensWeb.dll's bytes,
# which makes it part of tools/verify_il_identical.py's hash.
#
# Without a rule here that is decided by core.autocrlf plus whatever wrote the
# file last, and it drifts silently: git reports such a file as modified but
# prints an EMPTY diff (the blob is identical), which reads as noise and gets
# ignored -- and then the oracle reports DIFFERENT for a provably cosmetic
# change, because its reference side always comes from a FRESH checkout. That
# cost a full investigation once (card 6cdb7c62).
#
# crlf, not lf: it is what every checkout on the Windows dev box already
# produces, so pinning it moves nothing locally. Linux CI now checks these out
# as CRLF too, which is the point -- one deterministic answer everywhere.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto`: that touches every file class in the
# repo and needs its own card. Only the file types whose whitespace can reach
# the assembly belong here. .cshtml matches nothing today; it is listed so a
# future Razor Page cannot re-open the same trap.
*.razor   text eol=crlf
*.cshtml  text eol=crlf
